  "root_cause_classification": {
    "primary": "The legacy System Audit authority current read takes global SHARE NOWAIT relation locks across the 22-table runtime closure. When acquired inside a savepoint or nested atomic block, PostgreSQL retains them until the outer transaction ends, expanding unrelated writer conflicts beyond one selector.",
    "preflight_publication_race": "A real TOCTOU risk exists when authority is checked before a later publication transaction, but the historical 1.7951-second failure ended at initial authority preflight before provider, writes, or publication. No publication writer or ungranted lock was observed in this read-only sample, so publication self-race is not the cause established for that failure.",
    "remaining_forensics_limit": "The exact historical blocker PID, SQL and relation were not retained. Broad exception mapping collapsed relation-lock conflict, advisory-lock conflict, connection failure, decoding failure and genuinely non-current authority into one external code."
  },
